-- SOP-506 (Operating the Scales — Weighing Ingredients) — populate + number the existing draft row.
--
-- An empty draft titled "The Weighing Station" (id 72ec9f6e-1d4c-4630-a8cd-0af15304027c, sop_number null, null content) already
-- existed in Job-Specific Operations. Repurpose it rather than insert a duplicate: assign SOP-506 (next
-- free Production 500s number after SOP-501..505), retitle, and write the structured operation body.
--
-- Covers both ingredient bench scales (OHAUS Defender 3000 i-DT33 + a second bench scale, model TBC).
-- SQF 11.2.3 (Calibration): calibration is periodic by QA / an approved provider — NO daily operator
-- check (removed per owner: they do not calibrate daily); a scale that reads wrong is tagged out and
-- reported. Content written WITHOUT arrow glyphs (clean pdfmake/Roboto PDF). status stays draft.
--
-- Row is draft, so the sop_documents_history snapshot trigger does not fire. Idempotent on id.

update public.sop_documents set
  sop_number    = 'SOP-506',
  title         = 'Operating the Scales (Weighing Ingredients)',
  type          = 'sop',
  category      = 'Job-Specific Operations',
  status        = 'draft',
  revision      = 'New',
  sqf_reference = '11.2.3.1, 11.2.3.6',
  sqf_required  = true,
  content       = $json${"purpose":"To weigh ingredients accurately to the batch sheet.\n\nTwo things drive the rules below. The weight decides the formula \u2014 a scale that reads wrong means wrong quantities, which is a formulation and allergen risk (too much or too little of an ingredient, including allergens). And the platform contacts food and food containers, so it must be kept clean and free of foreign matter.","scope":"Production staff weighing ingredients on the bench scales.\n\nCalibration (adjusting the scale against certified reference weights) is done by QA or an approved calibration provider on a schedule \u2014 not by operators. If a scale reads wrong or is damaged, operators tag it out and report it rather than adjust it.","responsibility":"Operators \u2014 level/clean check, power on to a stable zero, confirm the unit, tare and weigh to the batch-sheet target, keep the platform clean, and tag out and report a scale that reads wrong or is damaged.\nSupervisor / QA \u2014 maintain the scale calibration program and the equipment directory, arrange periodic calibration, and resolve an out-of-calibration scale and any product weighed on it.","procedure":["Before you start: the scale sits on a level, stable, vibration-free surface; the platform is clean, dry, and clear of foreign matter, spilled product, and debris. Power on: press and hold On/Zero (about 2 seconds) and let the scale settle to a stable zero; if it does not sit at zero with an empty platform, press Zero (must be stable). Confirm the weighing unit (kg / g / lb / oz) matches the batch sheet \u2014 press and hold Units to change it. Weighing in the wrong unit is a common error.","Weigh into a container (tare): place the empty container on the platform and press Tare \u2014 the display returns to zero (net) and stores the container weight. Add the ingredient until the display reaches the target weight on the batch sheet; read the value only when the stable indicator is showing (the reading has settled). Use a food-safe container, do not overload past the scale capacity, and keep the load centered on the platform. To clear the tare, remove everything and press Tare again (display returns to gross zero).","Weighing to a target: read only a stable reading \u2014 a drifting number is not a valid weight. On the OHAUS Defender, Check mode (if set up) shows green when the weight is in the target range, yellow under, red over \u2014 a quick visual confirm that does not replace reading the number. Double-check the unit and the target against the batch sheet before you commit the ingredient.","Allergen care: clean the platform and the container between allergen ingredients. Brush or wipe spilled powder off the platform so it is not carried into the next ingredient (allergen cross-contact).","After weighing and cleaning: power off with a long press of Off (or leave on if auto-off is set). Disconnect / unplug before wet cleaning; wipe the platform and surround with a clean damp cloth and do not let water into the indicator or connections. Remove and clean the pan if fitted.","If something goes wrong: Will not hold zero \u2014 remove all weight, make sure the platform is clean/dry and stable, then press Zero. Reading drifts or will not stabilize \u2014 check for draft, vibration, a wet or overloaded platform, or something touching the pan; fix and re-check. Reading looks wrong or you doubt its accuracy \u2014 tag Do Not Use, weigh on another scale, and tell the Supervisor; do not adjust the scale (QA verifies it against certified weights). Scale dropped, knocked, or overloaded \u2014 tag it out and have QA verify it before it is used again. Wrong unit shown \u2014 press and hold Units until the batch-sheet unit appears."],"form_references":"Batch / recipe sheet (target weights for each ingredient). Scale calibration records (periodic calibration by QA / an approved provider).","records":"Calibration certificates / records from the periodic calibration are kept by QA, and a directory of measuring equipment that requires calibration is maintained (SQF 11.2.3.6). Operator training sign-off is held in the training record. All retained per the record retention policy.","governing_reference":"SQF Food Safety Code: Food Manufacturing, Edition 9 \u2014 11.2.3.1 (documented calibration methods and responsibility), 11.2.3.3 (per manufacturer schedule), 11.2.3.4 (resolution of product when equipment is out of calibration), 11.2.3.6 (equipment directory and calibration records).\nOHAUS \u2014 Defender 3000 (i-DT33) Quick Start Guide, P/N 30696557.\nSecond scale \u2014 operation manual to be added once make/model is confirmed.","revision_history":"New \u2014 2026-07-27 \u2014 Initial issue. Covers both ingredient bench scales (OHAUS Defender 3000 i-DT33 + a second bench scale, model TBC). Weighing process: level/clean check, power to stable zero, confirm unit, tare the container, add to the batch-sheet target, read only when stable, allergen cleaning between ingredients, wipe-down with the indicator kept dry. Calibration is periodic by QA / an approved provider (no daily operator check); a scale that reads wrong is tagged out and reported. SQF 11.2.3 (Calibration) basis; OHAUS i-DT33 quick guide referenced."}$json$::jsonb
where id = '72ec9f6e-1d4c-4630-a8cd-0af15304027c';

insert into supabase_migrations.schema_migrations (version, name)
values ('20260727000005', 'sop506_ingredient_scales_operation')
on conflict (version) do nothing;
